	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Hillsbrad Foothills are the green southern marches of the old kingdom of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. They run from the snows of the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link} down to a mild coast on the sea. The plague that killed Lordaeron passed them by, and for a little while Hillsbrad seemed spared. It was not. Today the foothills are a battlefield. The humans of {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} hold the coast, the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} hold {link:tarren-mill}Tarren Mill{/link} in the north, and between them the farms of Hillsbrad burn one by one.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the first villages rose in these hills. They were part of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} for as long as that kingdom stood. On the eastern border stands the ancient wall that bears the name of {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, the founder of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}. When {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} fell in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, its refugees came ashore at {link:southshore}Southshore{/link}, and Hillsbrad was the first land of the north to greet them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Hillsbrad is caught between two wars. {link:high-executor-darthalia}High Executor Darthalia{/link} commands the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of {link:tarren-mill}Tarren Mill{/link} in the name of {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link} and {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link}. Her Deathguard raid the farms of {link:hillsbrad-fields}Hillsbrad Fields{/link}, and the apothecaries of the {link:royal-apothecary-society}Royal Apothecary Society{/link} test their new poisons on the farmers and their animals. {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} and the dwarves of {link:dun-garok}Dun Garok{/link} answer with the few soldiers they have. Meanwhile the {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link} preys on both sides from the ruins of {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde Keep{/link}. Its assassins are believed to have murdered one magistrate of Southshore already, and they are hunting the next. {link:orcs}Orcs{/link} sent by {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} himself have lately come to Tarren Mill, for Durnholde was once the Warchief's prison, and he wants something back from it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The people of {link:southshore}Southshore{/link}.{/b} Fishermen, soldiers and scholars, loyal to the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.
• {b}The farmers of Hillsbrad.{/b} They still work the fields west of the river, under the eyes of the enemy.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Their Deathguard, Deathstalkers and apothecaries hold {link:tarren-mill}Tarren Mill{/link}.
• {b}{link:orcs}Orcs{/link} of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} A small band sent from {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}, and a smith who works quietly at Tarren Mill.
• {b}The dwarves of {link:dun-garok}Dun Garok{/link}.{/b} A garrison of {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} in the south-east, sworn to defend the humans and their mine.
• {b}The {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link}.{/b} Thieves and shadow mages in the service of the fallen lords of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}.
• {b}Beasts and raiders.{/b} {link:murlocs}Murlocs{/link} on the {link:western-strand}Western Strand{/link}, {link:naga}naga{/link} on the {link:eastern-strand}Eastern Strand{/link}, {link:gnolls}gnolls{/link} at {link:nethander-stead}Nethander Stead{/link}, and ogres who come down from Alterac.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Refugees.{/b} After the fall of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, the survivors crossed the sea and landed at {link:southshore}Southshore{/link}. From there, word of the orcs was carried to King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link}.
• {b}The Second War.{/b} {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} gathered the armies of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} in Hillsbrad. The {link:horde}Horde{/link} landed near Southshore, and here the two hosts met in the first great land battle of the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. Here too the death knights of the Horde first faced the paladins of {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link}.
• {b}The Camps.{/b} After the war, {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde Keep{/link} became the seat of the camps where the defeated orcs were held. In its halls a young {link:orcs}orc{/link} named {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} was raised as a slave. He escaped, returned at the head of a new Horde, and brought the keep down in ruin.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} is gone, and even its southern hills are slipping from human hands.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Foothills",
			text = [=[• The folk of {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} say their cooks are the best north of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. Travellers from as far as {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link} have come for a bowl of Chef Jessen's turtle bisque.
• A wizard named {link:helcular}Helcular{/link} lies buried in the Southshore graveyard. He was killed by a mob of townsfolk before his dark ritual was done. Some in {link:tarren-mill}Tarren Mill{/link} mean to finish it.]=],
		},
	},
})

