			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Aedelas Blackmoore was the lord of {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde Keep{/link} and the master of the camps where the defeated orcs were held after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. He was a hard fighter, a heavy drinker and a man of great ambition. He found an orphaned {link:orcs}orc{/link} infant in the wild and raised him as a slave. That orc was {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}. Blackmoore meant him to be a weapon. Instead, Thrall became the Warchief who freed the orcs and killed him.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Blackmoore is the man who made {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, in every sense he did not intend. His cruelty taught the young {link:orcs}orc{/link} what humans could be. The kindness of others in his own household taught Thrall that they could be something else. Without Blackmoore there would have been no Thrall, and without Thrall no new {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Son of a Traitor",
			text = [=[Blackmoore fought well in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} and was known for his fury against the orcs. Yet he bore a heavy name. His father had been convicted of treason, and the whispers followed the son all his life. He drank to face battle, and he drank more when the war was over. When he was given {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde{/link} and the camps, his power grew, and so did his vices.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Orc Child",
			text = [=[While hunting with his servant Tammis Foxton, Blackmoore found an {link:orcs}orc{/link} infant among the bodies of his murdered parents. He carried the child to {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde{/link} and named him {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}. He had the boy taught to read, to write and to fight, and he sent him into {link:gurubashi-arena}the arena{/link} against the champions of other lords. In private, he dreamed of more. Thrall would one day lead an army of orcs from the camps, and through him Blackmoore would rule. He was often cruel to the boy and sometimes kind, and he never saw the difference as Thrall did.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Fall of Durnholde",
			text = [=[{link:thrall}Thrall{/link} escaped with the help of Tammis's daughter, {link:taretha-foxton}Taretha Foxton{/link}, whom Blackmoore had made his mistress against her will. Years later the {link:orcs}orc{/link} returned at the head of a free {link:horde}Horde{/link} and broke the camps one after another. On the night before the siege, Blackmoore learned that Taretha had met Thrall in secret. He had her put to death. When Thrall came to parley at the gates, a drunken Blackmoore cast her head down from the walls. The orcs stormed the keep. Thrall found Blackmoore inside and slew him in single combat. Then he called upon the spirit of the earth, and {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde{/link} fell upon its master's body.]=],
